    "solution": "Load the Home spring and use its return to jump right onto the low relay. Your landing raises that lift, lowers the far lift, and moves the labelled shutter into the upper light duct. Walk to the hanging hinge, climb it and cut its hub downward from above. Cross its new horizontal span to the western upper tally, then return over the same arm and jump to the eastern gallery. Turn the far mirror from its left side. The light is prepared but still blocked by the relay shutter. Drop around the eastern ledge onto the lowered far relay: this landing exchanges both lifts and clears the optical duct, lighting the sealed second receiver and opening the starting-side gate. Leave the far lift to the lower return conveyor. Load the same Home spring again and launch left, over the protected gallery edge, into the open home exit.",
    "nearestExisting": "B35 supplies the reusable recoil lift, B11/B12 supply a climbing arm that becomes a bridge, and B31 supplies a changed optical return. Here two opposed lifts and their shared optical shutter trade positions together: the first landing grants ascent, the far landing completes a circuit and returns the near lift below.",
    "novelty": "The recoil spring is a shared origin with two different destinations. Landing changes three remote pieces of geometry at once, so the ascent temporarily obstructs its own exit circuit. A permanent hinge conversion creates an upper return bridge, while the opposite relay landing completes the prepared light circuit and makes the homeward trip possible.",
